Task 84 adversarial pass (executor-run). Each class names the shipped test that guards it.

1. Fragmentation: a graphics header or terminator split across reads.
   vt engine::images::tests::chunking_never_changes_which_images_are_retained_or_where
   (the same stream fed whole and one byte at a time gives an identical ImageSet).
2. Key agreement between VT and gate: both must key a Kitty series by its first chunk,
   including a series that other output interrupts.
   vt ...::a_kitty_series_is_one_image_keyed_by_its_first_chunk_even_when_interrupted
   server streams::graphics::replay::tests::an_interrupted_kitty_series_is_one_key_measured_against_the_cap_together
3. Aggregate cap evasion (T83 seam a): runs of an interrupted series are measured together;
   one notice is placed at the series start, and the dropped series leaves the store.
   Same server test; killed mutant mutant-series-not-carried.log.
4. Scrolled-out images must not be re-sent: the anchor row is followed by the address of its
   cell buffer, so rows that rotate into scrollback are found missing.
   vt ...::the_anchor_follows_scrolling_and_leaves_with_the_visible_screen;
   server replay_a_scrolled_off_image_is_not_replayed; conformance graphics/replay failure.
   Killed mutant mutant-scrolled-out-never-released.log.
5. Recycled rows: a region scroll below the top resets and reuses a row buffer at another
   line. The anchor-cell mark (flag bit 15, which alacritty never defines) is reset with it.
   vt ...::a_region_scroll_moves_a_surviving_anchor_and_releases_a_recycled_one.
   Address reuse after a free is also covered: a new row is blank, so it carries no mark.
6. Erase/overwrite (ED, EL, ECH, a printed char): mark lost -> released; neighbours keep it.
   vt ...::erasing_or_printing_over_the_anchor_cell_releases_it_and_neighbours_do_not;
   server replay_a_cleared_screen_replays_no_image.
   Finding: alacritty's ED 2 moves the top row into scrollback (Grid::clear_viewport), so
   the first image reports scrolled_out and the rest report erased. The tests pin this.
7. Kitty a=d targets and case: id, number, all; lower case keeps a=t data, upper case
   removes it. Unknown targets are treated as "all", so nothing deleted is ever re-sent.
   vt ...::kitty_deletes_name_ids_numbers_and_placements_or_data_by_case;
   server replay_a_kitty_delete_removes_only_the_named_image.
   Killed mutant mutant-kitty-delete-ignores-id.log.
8. Id reuse: a transmission with an existing id releases the old image.
   vt ...::a_transmission_reusing_an_id_replaces_the_old_image
9. RIS and alternate screen: RIS releases all. Leaving 1049 releases the alternate images
   and keeps the primary ones. While the alternate screen is active, primary images are
   spliced into the primary part of the paint (before ?1049h).
   vt ...::ris_releases_every_image, ...leaving_the_alternate_screen..., tests::paint::primary_images_are_spliced...
10. Lookalikes are never retained or replayed: iTerm2 inline=0, OSC 1337 SetUserVar,
    DECRQSS DCS $ q, Kitty a=q, sixel with 64+ parameter bytes.
    vt ...::only_displayed_graphics_are_retained_never_their_lookalikes;
    server ...::an_osc_1337_that_is_not_an_inline_file_is_not_graphics,
    kitty_keys_are_read_up_to_256_bytes..., sixel_parameters_are_read_up_to_63_bytes.
    These kill the three surviving T83 mutants (mutant-t83-*.log).
11. Unbounded growth: the store is bounded by graphics_terminal_store_max_bytes with
    oldest-first eviction and a typed in-stream graphics_evicted record. The VT retains at
    most IMAGE_LIMIT=1024 images. The released lists are bounded (VT 4096, store 64).
    core terminals::images::tests::* (7); server replay_a_full_store_evicts_the_oldest_with_typed_counts;
    vt ...::the_engine_retains_at_most_its_image_limit. Killed mutant mutant-store-evicts-newest-first.log.
12. Replay storms: replayed bytes are shared Arc pieces of the store. They are not charged
    to the 4 MiB stream backlog or the session budget (Viewer::charged_backlog), so a 32 MiB
    replay cannot trigger an immediate gap+checkpoint loop.
    server ...::a_paint_shares_the_store_bytes_where_its_images_go (piece flags);
    killed mutant mutant-replay-not-spliced.log.
